that raises the quill when the porcupine gets nervous.

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:49.960
If the quill is touched even lightly by, say, a lion,

00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:53.000
it can easily rip free and gets pulled right out.

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:55.440
Thanks, Quilber.

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:56.000
Oh!

00:18:57.230 --> 00:18:57.630
Huh?

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.120
Won't be long, guys.

00:19:01.480 --> 00:19:03.360
Porcupine power disks on the way!

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:11.680
Good, because we've got some floating animals to rescue.

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:21.010
Get boots ready to go.

00:19:21.170 --> 00:19:26.370
All right, Quilber, my pointy little pal.

00:19:26.690 --> 00:19:28.990
Give us that porcupine defense power!

00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:42.430
Activate all set flying porcupine bros. Oh watch where you're swinging those quills. Oh, sorry, Jimmy

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:57.590
Can't take all these creatures and turn them into your robots. Yeah, and they don't like being in the sky. They want to go home

00:19:57.620 --> 00:19:59.760
Oh, no, you don't wild rat

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:01.920
It's Wild Kratz!

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:04.710
Whatever! I'll do whatever I want!

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:08.480
And guess what? My Zackbots are recharged!

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:10.710
Go!

00:20:11.010 --> 00:20:15.610
Uh-oh! Gotta get to those creatures!

00:20:16.750 --> 00:20:17.370
I'll cover you!

00:20:23.130 --> 00:20:24.390
Go off, Zackbots!

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:27.000
We porcupines don't like to use our quills!

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:28.730
But if we have to...

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:32.540
All right, I warned you.

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:38.680
Whoa, lost a few quills in that defense.

00:20:39.230 --> 00:20:40.250
Chris has better hurry.

00:20:45.230 --> 00:20:46.910
Don't worry, you're going home.

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:49.340
It's the porcupine power.

00:20:53.930 --> 00:20:55.150
Enjoy the ride, pal.

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:58.360
I'm gonna at you guys.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:04.880
No problem, we're off your maze.

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:09.010
You're ruining my part!

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:12.400
Knock those brothers out of the sky, Sackbots!

00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:14.200
Hang tight, Warthog.

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:18.650
Uh-oh, Sackbot coming in fast!

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:19.670
I'll slow it down.

00:21:19.870 --> 00:21:21.340
Got it.

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:27.040
Oh, still have some quills left.

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:28.900
Four balloons should do it.

00:21:30.250 --> 00:21:31.970
That'll take you down nice and easy.

00:21:32.170 --> 00:21:39.400
At least lions learn their lesson.

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:41.080
Zackbots don't.

00:21:41.560 --> 00:21:47.800
Oh, sorry, Zack, your party's over.

00:21:47.940 --> 00:21:49.500
Give me my varmints back!

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:54.910
And last but not least, that's all of them.

00:21:55.150 --> 00:21:56.230
Just in time.

00:21:56.660 --> 00:21:58.620
Oh, I have no quills left.

00:21:58.760 --> 00:21:59.540
I'll shoot you!

00:21:59.720 --> 00:21:59.980
Look at him!

00:22:01.020 --> 00:22:07.300
So tough without your quills, are you?

00:22:09.100 --> 00:22:09.680
What was that?

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:13.190
Oh, maybe I had one quill left after all.

00:22:13.470 --> 00:22:25.070
Loop-de-loop rides.

00:22:26.180 --> 00:22:28.000
Don't like loop-de-loop rides!

00:22:33.100 --> 00:22:34.260
Mission accomplished!

00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:37.060
We got the creatures back to where they belong.

00:22:37.530 --> 00:22:40.570
And Quilber's porcupine quilt event saved the day!

00:22:40.970 --> 00:22:44.430
And we finally got the decorations up for Aviva's birthday!

00:22:45.010 --> 00:22:48.190
And we finally finished the present we wanted to get for you!

00:22:48.820 --> 00:22:50.360
Happy birthday, Aviva!

00:22:51.030 --> 00:22:52.830
Now that's how you wrap a present!

00:22:54.780 --> 00:22:57.180
You made my quills into a necklace!

00:22:57.990 --> 00:22:58.650
I lit!

00:22:59.680 --> 00:22:59.980
Thanks for that!

00:23:00.090 --> 00:23:02.930
And thank you, too, Quilbert.

00:23:03.170 --> 00:23:04.410
Hey, now for the cake.

00:23:05.260 --> 00:23:06.610
Really? What kind?

00:23:06.910 --> 00:23:09.290
Bark and root cake. What else?

00:23:09.800 --> 00:23:10.120
Huh?

00:23:10.630 --> 00:23:12.250
What's for the other birthday girls?

00:23:12.470 --> 00:23:15.470
The Porky Pet Sisters.

00:23:15.960 --> 00:23:17.800
They love bark and root cake.

00:23:18.690 --> 00:23:19.370
There you go.

00:23:21.860 --> 00:23:23.470
Happy birthday, Porky Pet!

00:23:28.860 --> 00:23:29.640
It's starting to harden.

00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:39.830
So, porcupine quills are an amazing example of nature's inventions, turning specialized

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:41.830
hair into a powerful defense.

00:23:42.090 --> 00:23:47.330
The quill defense is so successful, it protects 18 species of porcupine around the world.

00:23:48.820 --> 00:23:51.320
And each one of them is a little bit different.

00:23:51.940 --> 00:23:57.980
Take the North American porcupine and the African crested porcupines.

00:24:00.410 --> 00:24:01.870
How about those quills, huh?

00:24:02.230 --> 00:24:07.170
The North American porcupine lives in the trees and is a great tree climber.

00:24:08.280 --> 00:24:11.920
His sharp claws help him climb, and his tail gives him leverage.

00:24:12.980 --> 00:24:15.920
African crescent porcupines spend their time on the ground

00:24:15.920 --> 00:24:18.120
and live underground in holes.

00:24:18.340 --> 00:24:19.460
They're great diggers.

00:24:20.500 --> 00:24:22.200
Let's have a look at these quills.

00:24:22.500 --> 00:24:25.320
North American porcupines have shorter quills.

00:24:26.010 --> 00:24:28.510
And they're mixed in with all this fur.

00:24:29.140 --> 00:24:29.960
Now that's because they

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.580
They live in cold climates.

00:24:31.850 --> 00:24:35.190
They need this fur, especially in the fall and winter

00:24:35.190 --> 00:24:36.470
when it starts getting cold.

00:24:37.060 --> 00:24:41.520
African crested porcupines they don't need a lot of hair because they live where it's warm

00:24:42.470 --> 00:24:44.490
But I do like their long mohawk hairs.

00:24:46.280 --> 00:24:48.660
I just got to stay a quill's length away from him.

00:24:49.220 --> 00:24:51.140
Check out the quills up close

00:24:51.820 --> 00:24:53.740
North American porcupine quills.

00:24:54.060 --> 00:24:54.800
Have time?

00:24:55.110 --> 00:24:56.230
little barbs on them.

00:24:56.680 --> 00:24:58.720
so that when they stick in your skin,

00:24:59.400 --> 00:24:59.680
Au!

00:25:00.500 --> 00:25:02.440
The barbs hold them in there.

00:25:02.940 --> 00:25:06.240
African crested porcupines don't have barbs on their quills,

00:25:06.360 --> 00:25:08.820
but they have quills that rattle on the end,

00:25:09.080 --> 00:25:11.360
sending a warning, like as if these quills themselves

00:25:11.360 --> 00:25:12.200
aren't warning enough.

00:25:14.780 --> 00:25:16.020
When a predator's around.

00:25:16.220 --> 00:25:18.460
or a North American porcupine gets startled.

00:25:18.870 --> 00:25:21.150
This is what their raised quills look like.

00:25:24.340 --> 00:25:27.120
See, it exposes all the sharp quills.

00:25:27.580 --> 00:25:28.180
And then...

00:25:28.340 --> 00:25:29.920
You don't want to stick your nose in that.

00:25:30.280 --> 00:25:30.480
Thank you.

00:25:33.290 --> 00:25:33.690
Just me.

00:25:34.890 --> 00:25:36.730
The African Crested Porcupine?

00:25:37.030 --> 00:25:40.110
And the North American porcupine.

00:25:40.210 --> 00:25:43.390
And there's one thing all porcupines have in common.

00:25:44.230 --> 00:25:46.490
Porcupines don't shoot their quills.

00:25:46.670 --> 00:25:50.050
They just are very loose, and they come out easily

00:25:50.050 --> 00:25:52.270
and stick into whatever touches them.

00:25:52.350 --> 00:25:52.610
Whoa!

00:25:53.830 --> 00:25:55.190
It's just your food.

